lexical extraction
├── when extracting typescript lexically
│   ├── it matches the native extraction
│   └── it reports parameterized tests identically
├── when decoys hide in comments and strings
│   └── it matches the native extraction
├── when fuzzing random test files
│   └── it never diverges from the native extraction
├── when extracting rust lexically
│   └── it matches the native extraction
├── when fuzzing random rust files
│   └── it never diverges from the native extraction
├── when a raw name profile extracts declarations
│   └── it nests tests by bracket spans
├── when a scaffolded file is checked lexically
│   └── it reports no findings for hostile titles
├── when a lexical profile is malformed
│   └── it refuses to load
└── when the scanner cannot account for the source
    └── it fails closed
